---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../styles/context.css';
import { brainPrompt, corePrompt, filesPrompt } from '../data/prompts';

const description =
  'Connect the sources that already know you, then run one prompt that compiles them into a private knowledge wiki.';
---

<Layout minimal bodyClass="plain" title="Caleb Haymore | Context" description={description}>
  <a class="skip" href="#core">Skip to the prompt</a>
  <a class="home-link" href="/">Caleb Haymore</a>

  <main class="field">
    <h1 class="sr-only">Context</h1>
    <p class="intro">Upload the data from, or connect, each of these tools to one AI. Run the center prompt there. It structures everything into a format an agent can read.</p>

    <section aria-labelledby="web-title">
      <h2 id="web-title" class="sr-only">Sources around the core prompt</h2>
      <div class="web-stage" data-web>
        <article class="core" id="core">
          <p class="core-kicker">Run this once you've gathered all the context.</p>
          <div class="core-scroll">
            <pre id="core-prompt">{corePrompt}</pre>
          </div>
          <div class="core-foot">
            <button class="copy-btn" type="button" data-copy="#core-prompt">Copy prompt</button>
            <span class="gathered-count" data-gathered-count>0 of 7 gathered</span>
          </div>
        </article>

        <button class="node node-imessage" type="button" data-source="imessage" data-label="iMessage" data-role="core relationships" aria-label="iMessage, core relationships. Open instructions." aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-controls="source-dialog">
          <span class="logo" aria-hidden="true">
            <img src="/icons/imessage.png" alt="" width="225" height="225" />
          </span>
          <span class="node-caption">
            <span class="node-title">iMessage</span>
            <span class="node-role">Core relationships</span>
          </span>
        </button>

        <button class="node node-linkedin" type="button" data-source="linkedin" data-label="LinkedIn" data-role="wider network" aria-label="LinkedIn, wider network. Open instructions." aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-controls="source-dialog">
          <span class="logo" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24">
              <path fill="#0A66C2" fill-rule="evenodd" d="M20.447 20.452h-3.554v-5.569c0-1.328-.027-3.037-1.852-3.037-1.853 0-2.136 1.445-2.136 2.939v5.667H9.351V9h3.414v1.561h.046c.477-.9 1.637-1.85 3.37-1.85 3.601 0 4.267 2.37 4.267 5.455v6.286zM5.337 7.433c-1.144 0-2.063-.926-2.063-2.065 0-1.138.92-2.063 2.063-2.063 1.14 0 2.064.925 2.064 2.063 0 1.139-.925 2.065-2.064 2.065zm1.782 13.019H3.555V9h3.564v11.452zM22.225 0H1.771C.792 0 0 .774 0 1.729v20.542C0 23.227.792 24 1.771 24h20.451C23.2 24 24 23.227 24 22.271V1.729C24 .774 23.2 0 22.222 0h.003z"></path>
            </svg>
          </span>
          <span class="node-caption">
            <span class="node-title">LinkedIn</span>
            <span class="node-role">People you know</span>
          </span>
        </button>

        <button class="node node-files" type="button" data-source="files" data-label="Files" data-role="on your computer" aria-label="Files on your computer. Open instructions." aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-controls="source-dialog">
          <span class="logo logo-files" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 72 58">
              <defs>
                <linearGradient id="folder-back" x1="36" y1="8" x2="36" y2="22" gradientUnits="userSpaceOnUse">
                  <stop stop-color="#7EB6FF"></stop>
                  <stop offset="1" stop-color="#4C97F6"></stop>
                </linearGradient>
                <linearGradient id="folder-front" x1="36" y1="20" x2="36" y2="56" gradientUnits="userSpaceOnUse">
                  <stop stop-color="#8EBEFF"></stop>
                  <stop offset="1" stop-color="#2B7FF0"></stop>
                </linearGradient>
              </defs>
              <path fill="url(#folder-back)" d="M8 18.5c0-2.4 1.9-4.3 4.3-4.3h12.2l4.2 4.3H59.5c2.5 0 4.5 1.9 4.5 4.3v3.2H8v-7.5z"></path>
              <path fill="url(#folder-front)" d="M5.2 24.2h62.2c1.8 0 3 1.6 2.5 3.3L62.6 51c-.5 1.8-2.1 3-4 3H14.2c-1.9 0-3.5-1.2-4-3L2.7 27.5c-.5-1.7.7-3.3 2.5-3.3z"></path>
              <path fill="#fff" fill-opacity="0.28" d="M8.5 27.2h55.2c.7 0 1.1.7.8 1.3l-1.2 2.2H9.2l-.7-3.5z"></path>
            </svg>
          </span>
          <span class="node-caption">
            <span class="node-title">Files</span>
            <span class="node-role">On your computer</span>
          </span>
        </button>

        <button class="node node-gmail" type="button" data-source="gmail" data-label="Gmail" data-role="correspondence" aria-label="Gmail, correspondence. Open instructions." aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-controls="source-dialog">
          <span class="logo logo-gmail" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg viewBox="52 42 88 66">
              <path fill="#4285f4" d="M58 108h14V74L52 59v43c0 3.32 2.69 6 6 6"></path>
              <path fill="#34a853" d="M120 108h14c3.32 0 6-2.69 6-6V59l-20 15"></path>
              <path fill="#fbbc04" d="M120 48v26l20-15v-8c0-7.42-8.47-11.65-14.4-7.2"></path>
              <path fill="#ea4335" d="M72 74V48l24 18 24-18v26L96 92"></path>
              <path fill="#c5221f" d="M52 51v8l20 15V48l-5.6-4.2c-5.94-4.45-14.4-.22-14.4 7.2"></path>
            </svg>
          </span>
          <span class="node-caption">
            <span class="node-title">Gmail</span>
            <span class="node-role">Correspondence</span>
          </span>
        </button>

        <button class="node node-calendar" type="button" data-source="calendar" data-label="Google Calendar" data-role="your time" aria-label="Google Calendar, your time. Open instructions." aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-controls="source-dialog">
          <span class="logo" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 200 200">
              <g transform="translate(3.75 3.75)">
                <path fill="#FFFFFF" d="M148.882,43.618l-47.368-5.263l-57.895,5.263L38.355,96.25l5.263,52.632l52.632,6.579l52.632-6.579 l5.263-53.947L148.882,43.618z"></path>
                <path fill="#1A73E8" d="M65.211,125.276c-3.934-2.658-6.658-6.539-8.145-11.671l9.132-3.763c0.829,3.158,2.276,5.605,4.342,7.342 c2.053,1.737,4.553,2.592,7.474,2.592c2.987,0,5.553-0.908,7.697-2.724s3.224-4.132,3.224-6.934c0-2.868-1.132-5.211-3.395-7.026 s-5.105-2.724-8.5-2.724h-5.276v-9.039H76.5c2.921,0,5.382-0.789,7.382-2.368c2-1.579,3-3.737,3-6.487 c0-2.447-0.895-4.395-2.684-5.855s-4.053-2.197-6.803-2.197c-2.684,0-4.816,0.711-6.395,2.145s-2.724,3.197-3.447,5.276 l-9.039-3.763c1.197-3.395,3.395-6.395,6.618-8.987c3.224-2.592,7.342-3.895,12.342-3.895c3.697,0,7.026,0.711,9.974,2.145 c2.947,1.434,5.263,3.421,6.934,5.947c1.671,2.539,2.5,5.382,2.5,8.539c0,3.224-0.776,5.947-2.329,8.184 c-1.553,2.237-3.461,3.947-5.724,5.145v0.539c2.987,1.25,5.421,3.158,7.342,5.724c1.908,2.566,2.868,5.632,2.868,9.211 s-0.908,6.776-2.724,9.579c-1.816,2.803-4.329,5.013-7.513,6.618c-3.197,1.605-6.789,2.421-10.776,2.421 C73.408,129.263,69.145,127.934,65.211,125.276z"></path>
                <path fill="#1A73E8" d="M121.25,79.961l-9.974,7.25l-5.013-7.605l17.987-12.974h6.895v61.197h-9.895L121.25,79.961z"></path>
                <path fill="#EA4335" d="M148.882,196.25l47.368-47.368l-23.684-10.526l-23.684,10.526l-10.526,23.684L148.882,196.25z"></path>
                <path fill="#34A853" d="M33.092,172.566l10.526,23.684h105.263v-47.368H43.618L33.092,172.566z"></path>
                <path fill="#4285F4" d="M12.039-3.75C3.316-3.75-3.75,3.316-3.75,12.039v136.842l23.684,10.526l23.684-10.526V43.618h105.263 l10.526-23.684L148.882-3.75H12.039z"></path>
                <path fill="#188038" d="M-3.75,148.882v31.579c0,8.724,7.066,15.789,15.789,15.789h31.579v-47.368H-3.75z"></path>
                <path fill="#FBBC04" d="M148.882,43.618v105.263h47.368V43.618l-23.684-10.526L148.882,43.618z"></path>
                <path fill="#1967D2" d="M196.25,43.618V12.039c0-8.724-7.066-15.789-15.789-15.789h-31.579v47.368H196.25z"></path>
              </g>
            </svg>
          </span>
          <span class="node-caption">
            <span class="node-title">Calendar</span>
            <span class="node-role">Your time</span>
          </span>
        </button>

        <button class="node node-drive" type="button" data-source="drive" data-label="Google Drive" data-role="notes and files" aria-label="Google Drive, notes and files. Open instructions." aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-controls="source-dialog">
          <span class="logo logo-drive" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 87.3 78">
              <path d="m6.6 66.85 3.85 6.65c.8 1.4 1.95 2.5 3.3 3.3l13.75-23.8h-27.5c0 1.55.4 3.1 1.2 4.5z" fill="#0066da"></path>
              <path d="m43.65 25-13.75-23.8c-1.35.8-2.5 1.9-3.3 3.3l-25.4 44a9.06 9.06 0 0 0-1.2 4.5h27.5z" fill="#00ac47"></path>
              <path d="m73.55 76.8c1.35-.8 2.5-1.9 3.3-3.3l1.6-2.75 7.65-13.25c.8-1.4 1.2-2.95 1.2-4.5h-27.502l5.852 11.5z" fill="#ea4335"></path>
              <path d="m43.65 25 13.75-23.8c-1.35-.8-2.9-1.2-4.5-1.2h-18.5c-1.6 0-3.15.45-4.5 1.2z" fill="#00832d"></path>
              <path d="m59.8 53h-32.3l-13.75 23.8c1.35.8 2.9 1.2 4.5 1.2h50.8c1.6 0 3.15-.45 4.5-1.2z" fill="#2684fc"></path>
              <path d="m73.4 26.5-12.7-22c-.8-1.4-1.95-2.5-3.3-3.3l-13.75 23.8 16.15 28h27.45c0-1.55-.4-3.1-1.2-4.5z" fill="#ffba00"></path>
            </svg>
          </span>
          <span class="node-caption">
            <span class="node-title">Drive</span>
            <span class="node-role">Notes and files</span>
          </span>
        </button>

        <button class="node node-brain" type="button" data-source="brain" data-label="Brain" data-role="never written down" aria-label="Brain, never written down. Open instructions." aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-controls="source-dialog">
          <span class="logo logo-brain" aria-hidden="true">
            <img src="/icons/brain.png" alt="" width="246" height="256" />
          </span>
          <span class="node-caption">
            <span class="node-title">Brain</span>
            <span class="node-role">Never written down</span>
          </span>
        </button>
      </div>
      </section>

    <p class="model-tip">Run these searches on a cheap model, like Sonnet or Luna.</p>
    <p class="fine-print">
      The folders follow <a href="https://gist.github.com/karpathy/442a6bf555914893e9891c11519de94f">Andrej Karpathy's LLM wiki</a>.
      Exports include other people, so keep the folder private.
    </p>
    <noscript><p class="model-tip">Enable JavaScript to open each source. The prompt can still be selected and copied.</p></noscript>
    <p id="context-status" class="sr-only" role="status"></p>
  </main>

  <dialog id="source-dialog" class="source-dialog">
    <div class="dialog-shell">
      <form method="dialog" class="dialog-close-row">
        <button class="dialog-close" type="submit" autofocus>Close</button>
      </form>

      <article class="panel" data-panel="imessage" hidden>
        <h2 id="panel-imessage-title">iMessage</h2>
        <p class="panel-kicker">Core relationships</p>
        <p>
          This is the record of the people you actually talk to. It has to be exported from a Mac
          that is signed into Messages. The iPhone has no full export.
        </p>
        <ol class="steps">
          <li>
            <div class="step-copy">
              On the Mac, open System Settings → Privacy &amp; Security → Full Disk Access. Turn it on
              for Terminal. Quit Terminal and open it again. The exporter cannot read Messages without this.
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <div class="step-copy">
              Install <a href="https://github.com/ReagentX/imessage-exporter">imessage-exporter</a>.
              If you don't have Homebrew, install it from <a href="https://brew.sh">brew.sh</a> first.
              <div class="cmd">
                <pre id="imessage-install">brew install imessage-exporter</pre>
                <button type="button" data-copy="#imessage-install">Copy</button>
              </div>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <div class="step-copy">
              Export the text, and leave the photos behind. A text folder is something a model can read.
              <div class="cmd">
                <pre id="imessage-cmd">imessage-exporter -f txt -o ~/Desktop/imessage-export</pre>
                <button type="button" data-copy="#imessage-cmd">Copy</button>
              </div>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <div class="step-copy">
              If that folder is enormous, run it again with a start date so the model can actually get through it.
              <div class="cmd">
                <pre id="imessage-recent">imessage-exporter -f txt -o ~/Desktop/imessage-export -s 2023-01-01</pre>
                <button type="button" data-copy="#imessage-recent">Copy</button>
              </div>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <div class="step-copy">When you run the center prompt, give it the <code>imessage-export</code> folder.</div>
          </li>
        </ol>
        <p>
          If the command cannot find the database, Messages in iCloud may still be downloading, or
          Full Disk Access did not stick. Restart Terminal after turning it on.
        </p>
        <div class="panel-actions">
          <button class="gather" type="button" data-gather="imessage" aria-pressed="false">Mark as gathered</button>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="panel" data-panel="linkedin" hidden>
        <h2 id="panel-linkedin-title">LinkedIn</h2>
        <p class="panel-kicker">The wider network</p>
        <p>
          Connections, messages, and the jobs you've had. This is the set of people you know who
          never became a text thread: work, school, and collaborators.
        </p>
        <ol class="steps">
          <li>
            <div class="step-copy">
              On a computer, open
              <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/mypreferences/d/download-my-data">Get a copy of your data</a>.
              The long way is Me → Settings &amp; Privacy → Data privacy → Get a copy of your data.
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <div class="step-copy">
              Request the larger data archive. Connections live in that archive. If your account still
              shows a separate Connections checkbox, select that too.
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <div class="step-copy">
              LinkedIn emails you when the download is ready. It often arrives the same day. They allow up to 24 hours.
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <div class="step-copy">
              Unzip it. <code>Connections.csv</code> is the file that matters most. Also keep messages,
              profile, and positions if they are in the archive. The csv usually has a notes preamble
              above the real header. The center prompt knows to skip it.
            </div>
          </li>
          <li><div class="step-copy">Give the unzipped folder to the center prompt.</div></li>
        </ol>
        <div class="panel-actions">
          <button class="gather" type="button" data-gather="linkedin" aria-pressed="false">Mark as gathered</button>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="panel" data-panel="files" hidden>
        <h2 id="panel-files-title">Files</h2>
        <p class="panel-kicker">Documents on your computer</p>
        <p>
          Notes, school, work, and the writing that never made it into email. Run this in a tool that
          can see the computer, on a cheap model like Sonnet or Luna. It should read the documents.
          It should not touch photos, apps, or caches.
        </p>
        <div class="panel-actions">
          <button class="copy-btn" type="button" data-copy="#files-prompt">Copy folder prompt</button>
        </div>
        <pre class="prompt-block" id="files-prompt">{filesPrompt}</pre>
        <div class="panel-actions">
          <button class="gather" type="button" data-gather="files" aria-pressed="false">Mark as gathered</button>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="panel" data-panel="gmail" hidden>
        <h2 id="panel-gmail-title">Gmail</h2>
        <p class="panel-kicker">Day-to-day correspondence</p>
        <p>
          Connect it. Don't export the whole mailbox. The center prompt assumes the tool you run it in
          can already read Gmail, and it only needs recent threads: what you are in the middle of,
          who you write, and what keeps coming back.
        </p>
        <ol class="steps">
          <li>Open the tool where you will paste the center prompt.</li>
          <li>
            Connect Gmail on the account you actually live in.
            In Claude that is Settings → Connectors. In ChatGPT it is Settings → Apps.
            In a coding agent, use a Google MCP server with Gmail enabled.
          </li>
          <li>Leave the connection on. You do not attach a mail file unless the tool has no connector.</li>
        </ol>
        <details class="fallback">
          <summary>No Google connection</summary>
          <p>
            Use <a href="https://takeout.google.com">Google Takeout</a> and export Mail. Takeout can also
            export Calendar and Drive in the same pass. An mbox of your whole inbox is huge. Prefer the
            connector, and only fall back to Takeout if the tool cannot connect.
          </p>
        </details>
        <div class="panel-actions">
          <button class="gather" type="button" data-gather="gmail" aria-pressed="false">Mark as gathered</button>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="panel" data-panel="calendar" hidden>
        <h2 id="panel-calendar-title">Google Calendar</h2>
        <p class="panel-kicker">How your time actually goes</p>
        <p>
          The calendar is better evidence than a self-description. Recurring events, who you meet,
          and which days are already spoken for.
        </p>
        <ol class="steps">
          <li>In the same tool, connect Google Calendar on the account you use.</li>
          <li>Claude: Settings → Connectors. ChatGPT: Settings → Apps. A coding agent: a Google MCP server.</li>
          <li>
            You don't export it. The center prompt reads the shape of your weeks, not every event you have ever had.
          </li>
        </ol>
        <p>
          If the tool cannot connect, <a href="https://takeout.google.com">Google Takeout</a> can export Calendar as well.
        </p>
        <div class="panel-actions">
          <button class="gather" type="button" data-gather="calendar" aria-pressed="false">Mark as gathered</button>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="panel" data-panel="drive" hidden>
        <h2 id="panel-drive-title">Google Drive</h2>
        <p class="panel-kicker">Notes, docs, and files</p>
        <p>
          Drive is where the unfiled writing lives: notes, journals, decks, and the documents from work
          that never made it into a message. Connect it. Do not hand over the entire drive.
        </p>
        <ol class="steps">
          <li>Connect Google Drive in the same tool, on the same account.</li>
          <li>Claude: Settings → Connectors. ChatGPT: Settings → Apps. A coding agent: a Google MCP server.</li>
          <li>
            The center prompt looks for folders that resemble notes, journals, writing, or active work.
            If it can't tell, it will ask you once which folders matter.
          </li>
        </ol>
        <p>
          If the tool cannot connect, export just those folders from
          <a href="https://takeout.google.com">Google Takeout</a> rather than all of Drive.
        </p>
        <div class="panel-actions">
          <button class="gather" type="button" data-gather="drive" aria-pressed="false">Mark as gathered</button>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="panel" data-panel="brain" hidden>
        <h2 id="panel-brain-title">Brain</h2>
        <p class="panel-kicker">Everything that was never written down</p>
        <p>
          Run this in a separate chat. It interviews you, one question at a time, for the likes,
          dislikes, people, and beliefs that are only in your head. When you are done, save the
          markdown it writes and give that file to the center prompt.
        </p>
        <div class="panel-actions">
          <button class="copy-btn" type="button" data-copy="#brain-prompt">Copy interview prompt</button>
        </div>
        <pre class="prompt-block" id="brain-prompt">{brainPrompt}</pre>
        <div class="panel-actions">
          <button class="gather" type="button" data-gather="brain" aria-pressed="false">Mark as gathered</button>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </dialog>

  <script>
    import '../scripts/context-web.ts';
  </script>
</Layout>
